20:34:04  MODEL OUTPUT  text         [coordinator] **Brief: Tessaly sodium-ion grid battery pilot at Kestrel Ridge**

**Performance**
- The pilot delivered 48 MWh of storage at peak demand in 2025, according to the year-one report (https://example.com/tessaly/year-one-results, p. 3).
- Round-trip efficiency averaged 87.4% (https://example.com/library/tessaly-safety-audit.pdf, p. 5).
- Capacity fade was 3.1% after the first year. This is an early indicator of lifespan and long-term cost (same audit, p. 7).

**Safety**
- No thermal runaway events were recorded across 1,200 charge cycles. That is a limited window for judging long-term safety (same audit, p. 2).

**Cost**
- A 2026 cost tracker puts Tessaly sodium-ion cells at $61/kWh at pack level (https://example.org/sodium-ion-cost-tracker-2026, p. 2). Only a snippet was seen, so the methodology is unverified.

**Expansion and funding**
- The Kestrel Ridge board approved $42 million for phase two in March 2026 (https://example.com/library/kestrel-ridge-board-minutes.pdf, p. 4).
- The utility plans a 300 MWh expansion by 2028, about six times the 48 MWh reported in year one (https://example.net/kestrel-ridge/news/tessaly-expansion, p. 1). This is a stated plan, not a completed result.

**Caveats**
- The web findings are medium confidence. The library findings are high confidence.
- The 48 MWh figure is the only operational output result found.
- I did not check whether the safety audit and the year-one report cover the same period.
